{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** You're given a sorted array in which every value appears **exactly twice**, except one value that appears **once**. Return that single value. Your solution must run in **O(log n)** time and **O(1)** space."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/1cb46f33-4ea6-4190-b6c8-10355ac0be56.svg",
      "alt": "1, 1, 2, 3, 3, 4, 4, 8, 8. Before the single value 2, each pair starts at an even index: the 1s at 0 and 1. After it, each pair starts at an odd index: the 3s at 3 and 4, the 4s at 5 and 6, the 8s at 7 and 8. So at an even index, a value equal to its right neighbour means the single one is further right; otherwise it's here or to the left.",
      "width": 794,
      "height": 368,
